course: dictionary
lesson: 7156
title: Performance: show, skill or doing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word performance can mean more than one thing, so the words around it tell you which meaning to use. «Stage fright, or performance nerves, is fear of performing.» Performing here means putting on a show, such as acting, singing or dancing for people to watch.
explain: «A test result is one day's performance, not a measure of your whole brain.» Here performance means how well you did on that day. The clue is test result: it tells you the word is about how well something went.
explain: Look for clues. A stage, an audience or a show points to the first meaning. A test, a match or a job points to how well someone did. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Performance can mean a show of acting, music or dance in front of an audience.
fact: Performance can also mean how well someone or something does a job or task.
fact: Performance can mean the act of doing something.
fact: «An appraisal, or performance review, is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year.»
fact: Useful phrases: give a performance, school performance, good performance.
exercise: «Stage fright, or performance nerves, is fear of performing.» Here, performance means | A loud engine noise | *A show of acting, music or dance in front of an audience | A meeting with the head teacher | A kind of paint
exercise: «A test result is one day's performance.» Here, performance means | A mistake you made on purpose | A dance step | A stage with bright lights | *How well you did on that day
exercise: Mum says, «The car's performance is good on steep hills.» What does performance mean? | A show for an audience | *How well the car works | A car park | The act of driving to the shop
exercise: «Feelings after a performance can be big and mixed.» What does performance mean here? | A boss's yearly meeting | How fast a machine works | *A show, such as a concert | A kind of mixed feeling
test: Ella will give a performance of a dance at the school hall. What does give a performance mean? | Write the dance down on paper | Forget the steps before the show | Stop dancing for good | *Show a dance to an audience
test: «Many famous performers say they still get stage fright, and it often fades once they start.» In this sentence, performers means | People who do their homework fast | *People who act, sing or dance for an audience | People who sell tickets | People who clean the stage
exam: «An appraisal, or performance review, is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year.» In this sentence, performance means | A new car engine | A loud noise from a machine | A dance in front of people | *How well someone has done at their job
